1. Definitions
--------------
"Personal Use" means use of the Software by an individual for their own
purposes, or by anyone strictly to evaluate whether to purchase a license.

"Commercial Use" means providing the Software, or access to it, to any
other person or organization as a paid product or service — including
selling installations, subscriptions, hosting, consulting packages, or
white-labeled versions of the Software — or use within an organization in
exchange for payment tied to the Software.

"License Key" means a cryptographically signed key issued by the Licensor
upon purchase (see tools/keygen.py and simon/licensing.py).

"Keygen" means the license-key generation tooling and its private signing
key (tools/keygen.py and any copy of the private key).

2. Grant for Personal and Evaluation Use
----------------------------------------
The Licensor grants you a royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable
license to use, copy, and modify the Software for Personal Use. No License
Key is required for Personal Use.

3. Commercial Use Requires a Purchased License
----------------------------------------------
Commercial Use is permitted only under a valid purchased License Key. The
scope of Commercial Use (number of seats, white-label rights, support
level) is defined by the plan purchased ("pro" or "business") and the
terms of sale. You may not use a License Key beyond its purchased scope,
and you may not share your License Key publicly.

4. Keygen and Private Key
-------------------------
You may not redistribute, publish, or share the Keygen or the private
signing key with anyone. Generating keys for others, or using leaked or
self-generated keys to evade Section 3, is a breach of this license.

5. Redistribution
-----------------
You may redistribute unmodified copies of the Software's source code only
if this LICENSE file is included intact. You may not redistribute modified
versions for Commercial Use except as permitted by a purchased plan.
Redistribution of the Keygen is prohibited under Section 4.

6. Third-Party Components and Services
--------------------------------------
The Software integrates with third-party services (LLM providers,
Telegram, Google, Home Assistant, and others). Those services are governed
by their own terms, which you must accept and comply with separately. The
Licensor provides no third-party API access.

7. No Trademark Rights
----------------------
This license grants no rights to the Licensor's names, logos, or
trademarks. References in documentation to third-party products are
descriptive only.

8. Termination
